[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Do you know what UV printing is? Because before we started filming this video, no one in my studio knew what it was. I did n\'t know that myself. So when Uvi approached me with an offer to sponsor a video about their UV printer, I couldn\'t immediately'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'agree because I simply didn\'t understand what it was. Can you send me this device? I had to check it out and see if I could come up with any interesting ideas for it . And it turned out that UV printing was something I did n\'t even know I always wanted.'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, what is UV printing? UV printing is a digital inkjet printing method that uses ultraviolet radiation to instantly set and harden liquid ink as it is applied to a'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'surface. Great, that sounds unimportant and general until you realize a few things. Firstly, the UV- cured ink is very bright and of incredible quality. It\'s like industrial'

[00:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'quality color printing. And there\'s a reason why it feels that way, because until recently, only manufacturers and factories could afford this kind of printing. Add to this the fact'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that thanks to the features of UV printing, you can layer white base resin, creating 3D effects. And besides, you can print on almost any surface: wood, ceramics,'

[01:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'plastic, metal, creating high-quality stickers, wall coverings or stained glass films. Suffice it to say that there are a lot of possibilities. So the question arises: what would I do with such a car? To'

[01:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'inspire you with ideas , Uvi supplies these printers with a set of printing materials to test the machine and get to know its operation. One such object is a rectangular ceramic'

[01:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'refrigerator magnet, on which I mastered the process of applying an image to an object while setting up the printer. So I applied our Gatecrash poster, where my characters jump out of a portal, and decided to try this 3D'

[01:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'effect that can be achieved using automatic adjustment. If you don\'t know how to create a height map, you can simply press a button to have the device identify the foreground, middle, and'

[02:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'background of the image to create a 3D embossing effect. I did this using a standard heightmap, and the result is an incredible 3D magnet. When you experience it for'

[02:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the first time, it\'s simply amazing. And you know you\'ve seen and held similar things in stores. Suddenly you realize: I can make things of this quality and produce them. And then I realized'

