[18:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'happy with my prototype before, but this…this is a whole other level. High-quality industrially produced cards, high-quality tiles, and the field… Well, the field itself. Okay, I said we\'re going back to the'

[18:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'playing field. We\'re going back to the field because there\'s one last thing I wanted to do. I have a nearly perfect prototype, except for that damn box, because any way I could think of to glue these four pieces together would have ruined the quality'

[19:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'or appearance of the box, but then I realized that with roll-to-roll printing I could make it look good and functional. In the UPrinting studio, I took my field, split it vertically in one copy, and duplicated it by splitting it horizontally in'

[19:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'another. UFE makes you go has all the tools you need to do a bunch of these things. So, to split something in half or into multiple pieces to print massive elements in vertical segments over multiple'

[19:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'prints, I switched from my canvas to polymer vinyl, which is essentially a large sheet of stickers, and placed copies of my game board into two oriented halves, printing everything in one go, and then'

[19:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'transferred that to another set of hexagonal board pieces, but this time I did something a little trickier. Using giant prints of the half-fields as huge stickers, I glued the two halves together'

[19:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as neatly and precisely as possible, then flipped them over to the other side, orienting them in a different direction. The result is a field'

[20:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that is laid out just like real playing fields. Guys, I\'m ready to cry. I am so happy. It\'s just incredible, and it took almost'

[20:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'zero extra effort to make it functional. I just glued them together and made one cut right here so it could fold in the opposite direction when closed. So now I have a fully functional, industrial-quality folding playfield. I'

[21:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can show it to anyone, play with anyone, and they won\'t be able to tell it was n\'t professionally made because the quality is incredible, it feels nice to the touch, and it functions perfectly.'

